# Every document, as the filing alone. One row per document, and one pool per row.
#
# The filing, never how much, and leaving it out is the point
#   examples/diagramming composes this and nothing wider, so the emitter cannot read a figure at
#   all. Which filing a pool is can be drawn and the figures cannot, and a diagram carries the
#   first. An emitter that could see a figure could render one, and a figure drawn in a notation
#   with no unit is the meaningless product entries/cross_layer_edges.sqlc names
#   `the_product_nobody_should_use`.
#
# A type error, not a design decision
#   Reading the wider relation does not compile: sqlx has no mapping for `pm.absence_reason`, and
#   needs a feature for NUMERIC. The schema refuses to hand a figure to a program with no use for
#   one, which is the DDL's typed blanks paying off in a second language.
-- epistemics/documents.sqlc projected to the filing alone; one pool per document.
SELECT d.filing
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/documents.sqlc)
) d
